Vendored VC4 command-list / shader validators (DARW-295 phase 2)
================================================================

Origin (permission to vendor given by the project owner, 2026-10-05):
  Mesa 25.2.8 (tag mesa-25.2.8, third_party/mesa), MIT licensed,
  Copyright 2014-2015 Broadcom, which mirrors Linux's
  drivers/gpu/drm/vc4 validators for userspace:
    src/gallium/drivers/vc4/kernel/vc4_validate.c
    src/gallium/drivers/vc4/kernel/vc4_validate_shaders.c
    src/gallium/drivers/vc4/kernel/vc4_render_cl.c
    src/gallium/drivers/vc4/kernel/vc4_packet.h
    src/gallium/drivers/vc4/kernel/vc4_drv.h
    src/gallium/drivers/vc4/vc4_qpu_defines.h
  The upstream license headers are kept in each file.

Written here (not from Mesa):
  vc4_simulator_validate.h  compat layer (replaces Mesa's file of that name)
  v3d_exec.[ch]             submit driver (replaces Mesa's kernel/vc4_gem.c;
                            follows Linux vc4_gem.c vc4_get_bcl())
  v3d_kglue.[ch]            the only interface the C++ driver sees (the
                            validator headers define macros such as max/min/
                            roundup/BIT that must not reach IOKit headers)

Why validators: the VC4 3D engine has no MMU/IOMMU; it DMAs whatever
addresses its command lists, shader records, uniforms and QPU programs
contain. Everything a client submits must be parsed, bounded against the
buffers it named, and rewritten with real GPU addresses before the GPU sees
it. Shader BOs are validated once at creation and are immutable afterwards.

Local modifications to the vendored files (each marked "V3D local fix" at
the site; found by comparing with current Linux and by the host tests in
tools/v3d_validate_test, ASAN + UBSan + fuzzing):

  vc4_validate.c
    - validate_gl_shader_rec(): shader handle bound was `> bo_count`
      (one-past-the-end BO read); now `>=`. The BO must also be a validated
      shader before validated_shader is dereferenced (NULL deref otherwise).
    - the remaining uniforms size was never decremented, so several shader
      records could together overrun the uniforms area.
    - the tile BO is created with drm_gem_cma_create_nostage() (no staging
      copy of megabytes of never-written memory).
    - the BO array in validate_gl_shader_rec() is fixed-size, not a VLA.
  vc4_render_cl.c
    - tile range vs. bin config: `>` -> `>=` (indices, not counts).
    - tile range is now also bounded by the render target size; with no bin
      CL the range was unconstrained and the hardware would store outside
      the surfaces whose size had been checked.
  vc4_validate_shaders.c
    - PROG_END in the last two instructions pushed max_ip past the BO end
      (out-of-bounds reads in both scans); now rejected.
    - raddr values 32..63 (uniform, varying, VPM...) were used as indices
      into the 68-entry live-register arrays; now untracked.
  vc4_qpu_defines.h
    - includes the compat header instead of Mesa's util/macros.h.
  vc4_validate_shaders.c: dropped #include "vc4_qpu.h" (unused here).

Known differences from Linux master (deliberate, not bugs):
  - tile state/alloc memory is a per-job BO (as in Linux 4.4 / Mesa's
    mirror) rather than Linux's shared binner BO with slots.
  - render-list MSAA full-res addressing uses exec->tile_width (Mesa's
    version); Linux uses a fixed 32. Equal for MSAA, which is the only
    case that emits those packets from Mesa.
  - Linux's later UBO "direct TMU" etc. fixes are present in this snapshot
    (is_direct); perfmon, fences and syncobjs are not used.

Testing: tools/v3d_validate_test/run.sh [iterations] [seed].
Not yet tested against Mesa's real vc4 output or on hardware.
